format-version: 1.2
date: 2023September20
default-namespace: Tripal Cultivate Germplasm Ontology
ontology: TRPC
idspace: TRPC https://knowpulse.usask.ca/cv/lookup/TRPC A collection of terms focused on supporting breeding-focused Tripal sites using the Tripal Cultivate package

[Term]
name: Germplasm Types
id: TRPC:TYPES
def: Terms used to categorize germplasm.
comment: This term should only be used within the ontology to provide hierarchy.

[Term]
name: F1 Seeds
is_a: TRPC:TYPES
id: TRPC:0001
def: After a female plant has been pollinated by a male plant as part of a manual cross, this term indicates the seeds collected from the female.
comment: This will typically in the USASK lentil breeding program have a name such as 12345a (i.e. a cross number). Our field crew also typically uses the same name/label for the seed packet and the plot they plant all these seeds in (i.e. F1 Plot).

[Term]
name: F1
is_a: TRPC:TYPES
id: TRPC:0002
def: The resulting plant from growing a single F1 seed.
comment: This will typically in the lentil breeding program have a name such as 12345a-1.

[Term]
name: F2 Seeds
is_a: TRPC:TYPES
id: TRPC:0003
def: These are the seeds from the F1 Plant and the process by which they were generated is indicated by the relationship between the F1 plant and the F2 seeds.
comment: For example, if the F1 plant was self fertilized then we would use a is_progeny_of_selfing relationship but if selection pressure was applied then we would use is_selection_of as the relationship. In the USASK Lentil breeding program the F2 seeds would typically have the same name as the F1 plant.

[Term]
name: F2
is_a: TRPC:TYPES
id: TRPC:0004
def: The resulting plant from growing a single F2 seed.
comment:

[Term]
name: F3 Seeds
id: TRPC:0005
is_a: TRPC:TYPES
id:
def: These are the seeds from the F2 Plant and the process by which they were generated is indicated by the relationship between the F2 plant and the F3 seeds.
comment: For example, if the F2 plant was self fertilized then we would use a is_progeny_of_selfing relationship but if selection pressure was applied then we would use is_selection_of as the relationship.

[Term]
name: F3
is_a: TRPC:TYPES
id: TRPC:0006
def:The resulting plant from growing a single F3 seed.
comment:

[Term]
name: F4 Seeds
is_a: TRPC:TYPES
id: TRPC:0007
def: These are the seeds from the F3 Plant and the process by which they were generated is indicated by the relationship between the F3 plant and the F4 seeds.
comment:

[Term]
name: F4
is_a: TRPC:TYPES
id: TRPC:0008
def: The resulting plant from growing a single F4 seed.
comment:

[Term]
name: F5 Seeds
is_a: TRPC:TYPES
id: TRPC:0009
def: These are the seeds from the F4 Plant and the process by which they were generated is indicated by the relationship between the F4 plant and the F5 seeds.
comment:

[Term]
name: F5
is_a: TRPC:TYPES
id: TRPC:0010
def: The resulting plant from growing a single F5 seed.
comment:

[Term]
name: F6 Seeds
is_a: TRPC:TYPES
id: TRPC:0011
def: These are the seeds from the F5 Plant and the process by which they were generated is indicated by the relationship between the F5 plant and the F6 seeds.
comment:

[Term]
name: F6
is_a: TRPC:TYPES
id: TRPC:0012
def: The resulting plant from growing a single F6 seed.
comment:

[Term]
name: F7 Seeds
is_a: TRPC:TYPES
id: TRPC:0013
def: These are the seeds from the F6 Plant and the process by which they were generated is indicated by the relationship between the F6 plant and the F7 seeds.
comment:

[Term]
name: F7
is_a: TRPC:TYPES
id: TRPC:0014
def: The resulting plant from growing a single F7 seed.
comment:

[Term]
name: F8 Seeds
is_a: TRPC:TYPES
id: TRPC:0015
def: These are the seeds from the F7 Plant and the process by which they were generated is indicated by the relationship between the F7 plant and the F8 seeds.
comment:

[Term]
name: F8
is_a: TRPC:TYPES
id: TRPC:0016
def: The resulting plant from growing a single F8 seed.
comment:

[Term]
name: Recombinant Inbred Line
is_a: TRPC:TYPES
id: TRPC:0017
def: A recombinant inbred line (RIL) population is developed through single seed descent from the F2 generation.
comment:

[Term]
name: Internal Accession
is_a: TRPC:TYPES
id: TRPC:0018
def: This is a type for parents of crossing blocks which we want to keep private. It is the default type used for parents of crosses unless we know they can be made public (i.e. material from genebanks or cultivars).
comment:

[Term]
name: Recombinant Inbred Line Population
is_a: TRPC:TYPES
id: TRPC:0019
def: A group of recombinant inbred lines (RIL) produced from a single cross.
comment: For example, the Recombinant inbred line population may be named LR-18 and indicates the full set of recombinant inbred lines (e.g. LR-18-2).

[Term]
name: Relationships
id: TRPC:RELATE
def: Terms used to describe relationships between two germplasm entities.
comment: This term should only be used within the ontology to provide hierarchy.

[Term]
name: progeny of selfing
is_a: TRPC:RELATE
id: TRPC:0020
def: This term is used to indicate the relationship between a parent germplasm and the progeny obtained from selfing it without selection involved. Specifically the subject is a population germplasm entry with a type such as F2 seeds and the object is the germplasm entry indicating the parent plant.
comment: In practice this term is only used to indicate the relationship between F1 seeds and the F1 plant. This is due to the genetic homogeny of all F1 seeds resulting from a specific cross. Whenever there is genetic hetrogeny in a population, we will use selection to indicate the relationship. This is due to the fact that the growth environment will place selection pressure on the seeds even if the researcher did not intend selection to occur.

[Term]
name: selection
is_a: TRPC:RELATE
id: TRPC:0021
def: This term is used to indicate the relationship between two germplasm entries where the object is the chosen individuals from the subject after a selection pressure is applied. As such the object is always a subset of the subject.
comment: One usage for this term is to indicate a chosen progeny individual (the subject; e.g. type F3 plant) after growing out a set of seeds (the object; e.g. F2 seeds). This relationship term may indicate conscious application of selection pressure (e.g. choosing a plant with low lodging occurance) or unconscious/unintended selection pressure (e.g. choosing the only plant which germinated or one which survived a naturally occuring disease)

[Term]
name: maternal parent
is_a: TRPC:RELATE
id: TRPC:0022
def: This term is used to indicate the relationship between a maternal parent (the subject; i.e. the plant producing seed in a sexual cross) and the seeds collected (the object; type F1 seeds).
comment: This term should not be used if it is later determined the resulting progeny do not include donor genetics but rather are the progeny of selfing. In this case the relationship term should be changed based on the new information to progeny of selfing. The object in this relationship will usually also have an additional relationship indicating the paternal parent. However, in cases where the pollen donor is unknown or suspected, only the maternal parent may be indicated via relationship.

[Term]
name: paternal parent
is_a: TRPC:RELATE
id: TRPC:0023
def: This term is used to indicate the relationship between a paternal parent (the subject; i.e. the plant donating pollen in a sexual cross) and the seeds collected from the cross (the object; type F1 seeds)
comment: This term should only be used if the pollen is collected from a donor parent plant and manually applied to the maternal parent plant. In all other cases we suggest including metadata on the cross indicating a suspected or intended pollen donor.

[Term]
name: recurrent parent
is_a: TRPC:RELATE
id: TRPC:0024
def: The parent (the subject) in a cross which provides the stable background (e.g. a cultivated variety) to reduce the genetic drag from the donor parent in the progeny (the object).
comment: For example, this terminology is most notably used in backcross situations where the donor parent is crossed with the recurrent parent and then the resulting progeny are repeatedly crossed with the recurrent parent.

[Term]
name: donor parent
is_a: TRPC:RELATE
id: TRPC:0025
def: The parent (the subject) in a cross which provides desired traits or introduces new genetic material to an exisiting germplasm to produce progeny (the object).
comment: For example, this terminology is most notably used in backcross situations where the donor parent is crossed with the recurrent parent and then the resulting progeny are repeatedly crossed with the recurrent parent.

[Term]
name: register cultivar
is_a: TRPC:RELATE
id: TRPC:0026
def: This term is used to indicate the relationship between the germplasm entry for a registered cultivar (the subject) and the original cross individual which was registered.
comment:

[Term]
name: extracted
is_a: TRPC:RELATE
id: TRPC:0027
def: This term is used to indicate relationship between the original plant material (the object) and the entry for a genetic extraction (the subject; e.g. DNA, RNA).
comment: For the USASK Lentil research group, we create entries to indicate the specific DNA sample which was sent for sequencing. This relationship is used to ensure we know if the phenotypic data was collected on the same germplasm which was sequenced or a genetically similar one.

[Term]
name: synonym
is_a: TRPC:RELATE
id: TRPC:0028
def: This term indicates that two germplasm entries are synonymous to each other.
comment: For the USASK Lentil breeding/research program we keep synonyms as separate germplasm entries and then associate them via relationship. This is done to keep in mind that although two entries may be very similar genetically, if they underwent seed increase in different environments they will have diverged slightly due to environmental selection pressure.

[Term]
name: Metadata
id: TRPC:METADATA
def: Terms used to describe additional information about a particular germplasm entity.
comment: This term should only be used within the ontology to provide hierarchy.

[Term]
name: F1 Seed Count
is_a: TRPC:METADATA
id: TRPC:0029
def: The number of seeds collected from this germplasm when it was at the F1 filial generation.
comment: For the USASK Lentil research program this term has historically been used to keep track of RIL individual seed counts at each generation.

[Term]
name: F2 Seed Count
is_a: TRPC:METADATA
id: TRPC:0030
def:The number of seeds collected from this germplasm when it was at the F2 filial generation.
comment: For the USASK Lentil research program this term has historically been used to keep track of RIL individual seed counts at each generation.

[Term]
name: F3 Seed Count
is_a: TRPC:METADATA
id: TRPC:0031
def: The number of seeds collected from this germplasm when it was at the F3 filial generation.
comment: For the USASK Lentil research program this term has historically been used to keep track of RIL individual seed counts at each generation.

[Term]
name: F4 Seed Count
is_a: TRPC:METADATA
id: TRPC:0032
def: The number of seeds collected from this germplasm when it was at the F4 filial generation.
comment: For the USASK Lentil research program this term has historically been used to keep track of RIL individual seed counts at each generation.

[Term]
name: F5 Seed Count
is_a: TRPC:METADATA
id: TRPC:0033
def: The number of seeds collected from this germplasm when it was at the F5 filial generation.
comment: For the USASK Lentil research program this term has historically been used to keep track of RIL individual seed counts at each generation.

[Term]
name: F6 Seed Count
is_a: TRPC:METADATA
id: TRPC:0034
def: The number of seeds collected from this germplasm when it was at the F6 filial generation.
comment: For the USASK Lentil research program this term has historically been used to keep track of RIL individual seed counts at each generation.

[Term]
name: F7 Seed Count
is_a: TRPC:METADATA
id: TRPC:0035
def: The number of seeds collected from this germplasm when it was at the F7 filial generation.
comment: For the USASK Lentil research program this term has historically been used to keep track of RIL individual seed counts at each generation.

[Term]
name: F8 Seed Count
is_a: TRPC:METADATA
id: TRPC:0036
def: The number of seeds collected from this germplasm when it was at the F8 filial generation.
comment: For the USASK Lentil research program this term has historically been used to keep track of RIL individual seed counts at each generation.

[Term]
name: Maternal Parent Number
is_a: TRPC:METADATA
id: TRPC:0037
def: The number designated to a maternal parent within a specified crossing block
comment: For the USASK Lentil breeding/research program, numbers are assigned to parents of a crossing block to keep track while out in the field. These numbers are commonly re-used each crossing block, and a parent can be used in multiple crossing blocks, so this number is specific to a particular crossing block season/year/parent combination only.

[Term]
name: Paternal Parent Number
is_a: TRPC:METADATA
id: TRPC:0038
def: The number designated to a paternal parent within a specified crossing block
comment: For the USASK Lentil breeding/research program, numbers are assigned to parents of a crossing block to keep track while out in the field. These numbers are commonly re-used each crossing block, and a parent can be used in multiple crossing blocks, so this number is specific to a particular crossing block season/year/parent combination only.

[Term]
name: Public
is_a: TRPC:METADATA
id: TRPC:0039
def: Indicates whether or not a germplasm is publicly accessible and not restricted to the breeding program
comment:

[Term]
name: Province of Origin
is_a: TRPC:METADATA
id: TRPC:0040
def: The province where the germplasm was originally found
comment:

[Term]
name: Market Class
is_a: TRPC:METADATA
id: TRPC:0041
def: A classification of a germplasm based on its characteristics that make it marketable to a particular set of consumers
comment: For the USASK Lentil research group in particular, we distinguish between market classes such as small red and large green, since consumers pay particular attention to the size and colour of the lentils they purchase.

[Term]
name: Variety Year Released
is_a: TRPC:METADATA
id: TRPC:0042
def: The year that a variety was registered and released.
comment:

[Term]
name: Source Institute
is_a: TRPC:METADATA
id: TRPC:0043
xref: CO_020:0000088 "FAO WIEWS code of the institute where the accession is maintained"
def: The institution (university, college, breeding group) this germplasm was developed or made available through.
comment: For the USASK Lentil research group, we use the following format for crossing blocks: [Season][Year]-P[parent number] where season is W-Winter, Sp-Spring, Sm-Summar, F-Fall.

[Term]
name: Crossing Block Parent
is_a: TRPC:METADATA
id: TRPC:0044
def: Indicates that the current stock was a parent in the indicated crossing block
comment:

[Term]
name: Country of Origin
is_a: TRPC:METADATA
id: TRPC:0045
xref: CO_020:0000013 "3-letter ISO 3166-1 code of the country in which the sample was originally collected, bred or selected"
def: The country where the germplasm was originally found
comment:

[Term]
name: Crossing Block Season
is_a: TRPC:METADATA
id: TRPC:0046
def: Indicates the season in which the current stock was the progeny of a cross
comment: For the USASK Lentil research group, we use the following format for crossing blocks: [Season][Year]-P[parent number] where season is W-Winter, Sp-Spring, Sm-Summar, F-Fall.

[Term]
name: Crossing Block Year
is_a: TRPC:METADATA
id: TRPC:0047
def: Indicates the year in which the current stock was the progeny of a cross.
comment: For the USASK Lentil research group, we use the following format for crossing blocks: [Season][Year]-P[parent number] where season is W-Winter, Sp-Spring, Sm-Summar, F-Fall.

[Term]
name: Cotyledon Colour
is_a: TRPC:METADATA
id: TRPC:0048
def: The color of cotyledon, which can be different from seed coat color.
comment:

[Term]
name: Seed Coat Colour
is_a: TRPC:METADATA
id: TRPC:0049
def: The color of the seed coat.
comment:

[Term]
name: Seed Type
is_a: TRPC:METADATA
id: TRPC:0050
def: A breeder assigned name for the seed category.
comment: This is usually similar to the market class, but more cotyledon/seed coat colour focused (e.g Red). If possible, as the breeder to supply the seed coat colour, cotyledon colour and market class instead. This should only be used for historical data.

[Term]
name: Breeding Method
is_a: TRPC:METADATA
id: TRPC:0051
def: The method used to generate or develop a germplasm.
comment: This can also be used by BrAPI as the breedingMethodDbId and then more details for the method would be retrieved via the /breedingmethods call.
